    <h1>About</h1>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      The New Bill of Rights project was started by
      <strong>Michael Hamilton</strong>, Founder. The foundation itself doesn't
      formally exist yet: incorporation as the New Bill of Rights Foundation is
      planned for 2026, and the
      <a href="/get-involved/seed-donors">founding donor round</a> is what
      starts it. As the founding board forms, directors will be listed here.
    </p>
    <p class="placeholder-note">Founder bio pending (workstream C4).</p>

    <h2>How this project works</h2>
    <p>
      Research → polling → salon → draft. Each category starts as an internal
      research document, gets tested against published cross-party polling,
      gets argued about in person, and only then becomes draft constitutional
      text — and only if it passes the full-spectrum bar. Everything, including
      what fails, is published in <a href="/evidence/rejected">the evidence</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="mailto:contact@newbillofrights.net">contact@newbillofrights.net</a>
    </p>
  </div>
